#: Implementation.md:1
msgid "Implementation"
msgstr "実装"

#: Implementation.md:3
msgid ""
"Small disclaimer: the code I am presenting here is a simplified version of "
"the actual code that is available as an example implementation in this "
"[repository](https://github.com/Iximiel/cudaOnPlumed). However for "
"production runs I would suggest to use the version that are hosted in the "
"main plumed repository, at time of writing this in version "
"[v2.10](https://github.com/plumed/plumed2/tree/v2.10/plugins/cudaCoord) or "
"the more updated version in "
"[master](https://github.com/plumed/plumed2/tree/master/plugins/cudaCoord) "
"these versions depend on C++17. The actual implementation has type templates"
" and supports pbcs. These particulars are not useful in understanding the "
"basis for a plumed implementation of a simple CV."
msgstr ""

#: Implementation.md:14
msgid ""
"If this is not the first time you read this I have updated the code on the "
"repository to use the NVIDIA's [CCCL](https://github.com/NVIDIA/cccl) API. "
"You may find some changes in the code. The code changes are not radical and "
"I may have missed something while updating the page, always refer to the "
"code present in the main [plumed "
"repository](https://github.com/plumed/plumed2/tree/master/plugins/cudaCoord)"
" for an up-to-date code."
msgstr ""

#: Implementation.md:21 Implementation.md:152
msgid "The switching function"
msgstr ""

#: Implementation.md:22
msgid ""
"In this case the coordination is calculated with $\\frac{1}{2} "
"\\sum_{i\\lt{}nat}^{i} \\sum_{j\\lt{}nat,j\\neq i}^{j} f(d_{ij})$, where "
"$d_{ij}$ is the distances between atom $i$ and $j$, and $f(x)$ is a function"
" that usually has the form"
msgstr ""

#: Implementation.md:35
msgid ""
"and $s(x)$ is a switching function that links smoothly 1 to 0 between $d_0$ "
"and $d_{max}$"
msgstr ""

#: Implementation.md:37
msgid ""
"In this case, I used the RATIONAL function like in the default Plumed "
"implementation: $s(r)=\\frac{ 1 - \\left(\\frac{ r - d_0 }{ r_0 "
"}\\right)^{n} }{ 1 - \\left(\\frac{ r - d_0 }{ r_0 }\\right)^{m} }$."
msgstr ""

#: Implementation.md:40
msgid ""
"But in this case, for simplicity, the implementation that I am showing will "
"not use the parameter $d_0$, so $s(r)=\\frac{ 1 - \\left(\\frac{ r }{ r_0 "
"}\\right)^{n} }{ 1 - \\left(\\frac{ r }{ r_0 }\\right)^{m} }$."
msgstr ""

#: Implementation.md:44
msgid ""
"Like in standard plumed implementation, the switching has a stretch "
"parameter: if $s(d_{max}) = shift $ and "
"$stretch=\\frac{1}{s(0)-s(d_{max})}$, $s(x)$ becomes "
"$s^s(x)=s(x)*stretch+shift$"
msgstr ""

